glimt: document it on the privacy page

Task 321, PRD 019 §6.

The copy lives in a module rather than in PrivacyView's template, because two of these
sentences are not prose. The Team-section reach is a disclosure the PRD requires to be
stated rather than discoverable, and a sentence in a template can be dropped by anyone
rearranging the page with nothing failing -- the reach is invisible by definition, so no
amount of looking at the page would show it had gone. The retention window carries a number
that must match the deployment, and it is only ever wrong on a deployment configured
differently from the developer's, which is exactly the case nobody looks at. The unit suite
never mounts a component, so copy left in the view could not be asserted at all.

The Team sentence says who they are and why. "Team kan se alle glimt" is true and useless;
this says "de voksne, der staar for loebet", gives the reason, and spells out the
consequence for the narrowest audience. It has to be unmissable and fair at once, or it
reads as surveillance rather than as the thing that makes the safety mechanism work.

Other decisions: the location is framed as what we do (the camera writes the place in and we
cut it out) rather than as what we lack, since it is the most reassuring true thing on the
page and the one a reader would never assume. "Ingen, der ser det igennem foerst" is stated
plainly, because with no approval queue in front of the public scope it is the fact a parent
most needs and would least expect. Hiding and deleting are kept distinct, so nobody is
surprised later.

glimtRetentionCopy returns an empty string when retention is off, and the view drops the
paragraph -- "0 dage" and "for altid" are both worse than silence about somebody's
photographs. Both windows are stated public-first, matching the order a parent asks.

Two guards beyond the copy: the view must still import every constant, since the module is
only a guarantee if the view renders it, and the view must hard-code no "N dage" of its own
-- the exact regression this task was written against, in the file most likely to
reintroduce it.

The tone has not been reviewed by a native Danish speaker, and should be: this is the only
written account most parents will see.
